1     Introduction
1.1     Background




                                                          型
    The Olympic Games are a global spectacle where nations vie for medals. While giants




                                                        模
like the USA and China lead the medal table, smaller countries such as Albania and
Cape Verde have made history, with both winning their ﬁrst gold medals at the 2024 Paris
Olympics. This highlights not just their growing sports prowess, but their rising prominence




                                                      学
on the world stage.




                                                    数
   Predicting future Olympic medal outcomes is complex. Current models often focus solely
on athlete performance and past results, missing key factors like national investments,
event changes, and shifting competition trends. A more comprehensive model could




                                                ：
greatly enhance predictions, particularly for the 2028 Olympics.




                                               el s
1.2     Problem Restatement
                                              号

                                             od
    We are provided with historical data on past Olympics, including host countries, events,
                               众
and detailed athlete performance, categorized by sport and medal type. The challenge is to



                                          Hm
build a model that can predict medal outcomes for the 2028 Olympics and provide insights
                    公

into the underlying factors.
                                       AT
   Task 1: Build a model to predict the total and gold medal counts for each country in
                   信


2028, with 90% conﬁdence intervals.
            微

                                      M

    • Compare the predictions with actual data from the 2024 Olympics to identify countries
      likely to see increases or decreases in their medal counts.
                           ：


    • Estimate the probability of each non-medal countries that will win their ﬁrst medals
      in 2028.
                          号




    • Explore the relationship between sports types, event numbers, and medal distributions
               信




      across nations.

    • Analyze the potential impact of new sports introduced by the host country on the
              微




      overall medal standings.

    Task 2: "The Great Coach Eﬀect"

    • Investigate the impact of great coaches on the medal performance of a nation, by
      examining changes before and after a coachs appointment.

    • Quantify the eﬀect of a coach’s inﬂuence on medal counts.

    • Identify three countries where hiring a coach could make a signiﬁcant diﬀerence in
      their performance.

    Task 3: Insights from the Model
Team # 2510006                                                                                                        Page 3


  • Explore the relationships between medal distributions, country-speciﬁc factors (e.g.
    sports events, economic development), and national strengths.

  • Help smaller countries optimize their medal chances despite resource limitations.

  • Explore the correlation between per capita medals and per capita GDP.




